4. Restrictions. You may not modify the Program, remove or change the author's notices, rebrand it, publish modified builds, or decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer it, except where applicable law expressly allows this despite this restriction, and except for rights you have under the licenses of third-party components listed in clause 6.

5. Content and your responsibility. The Program does not contain or provide any content. It is a neutral playback tool. You are solely responsible for the links, playlists, torrents, files, cameras and other sources you open with it, and for following the laws of your country, including copyright law. The author is not responsible for how you use the Program.

6. Third-party components. The Program uses third-party components under their own licenses, which stay in force and are not limited by this text: libmpv (LGPL-2.1 or later, https://mpv.io), libtorrent (BSD-3-Clause, https://libtorrent.org), anacrolix/torrent (MPL-2.0, https://github.com/anacrolix/torrent), Qt for Python / PySide6 (LGPL-3.0, https://doc.qt.io/qtforpython-6/), the face detection cascade from OpenCV (BSD-3-Clause, https://opencv.org), Python (PSF License, https://docs.python.org/3/license.html). Components the Program downloads at your request keep their own licenses too: FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org/legal.html). Country detection uses the "IP to Country Lite" data by DB-IP (CC BY 4.0, https://db-ip.com). The free films offered as examples are by the Blender Foundation (CC BY, https://studio.blender.org).

